            "question": "Calculate the bond order of Oxygen molecule ($O_2$) with 16 electrons.",
            "solution": "1. Molecular orbital configuration of $O_2$: $\\sigma_{1s}^2 \\sigma_{1s}^{*2} \\sigma_{2s}^2 \\sigma_{2s}^{*2} \\sigma_{2p_z}^2 (\\pi_{2p_x}^2 = \\pi_{2p_y}^2) (\\pi_{2p_x}^{*1} = \\pi_{2p_y}^{*1})$.\\n2. Count electrons: Bonding $N_b = 10$, Antibonding $N_a = 6$.\\n3. Bond Order: $BO = \\frac{10 - 6}{2} = 2$.",
