            "solution": "1. Convert $\\Delta S^circ$ to $\\text{kJ/mol K}$:$$\\Delta S^circ = -0.200\\text{ kJ/mol K}$$2. Use the Gibbs-Helmholtz relation:$$\\Delta G^circ = \\Delta H^circ - T\\Delta S^circ$$3. Substitute the values:$$\\Delta G^circ = -80.0\\text{ kJ/mol} - [298\\text{ K} \\times (-0.200\\text{ kJ/mol K})]$$$$\\Delta G^circ = -80.0 + 59.6 = -20.4\\text{ kJ/mol}$$Since $\\Delta G^circ < 0$, the reaction is spontaneous at $298\\text{ K}$.",
